    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A principality created in 1719 when the Liechtenstein family united Vaduz and Schellenberg to gain a seat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-diet">Imperial Diet</a>.</li><li>It outlived the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and the German Confederation, abolished its army in 1868 and tied itself to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in 1923.</li><li>A microstate of about 40,000 people, it combines strong princely powers with direct democracy and very high incomes.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The country is named after its ruling family, not the other way round: the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-liechtenstein">Liechtensteins</a> took their name from a castle south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, far from Vaduz.</p></aside>
    </section>

